From 94c17f845ea40d0f22b5c90725354516e8cefb93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:25:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/92] moe-stream : skip the pairs outside a prefill wave
 instead of parking them

LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_WAVE_SKIP=1, off by default, CUDA only, ubatches of 64 tokens and up.
Multi-pass prefill parked the pairs of the other waves on resident slots, ran them through
the expert GEMMs and zeroed them with a mask, so each of the 64 waves per layer multiplied
the whole ubatch. Skipped, a pair gets an id past the last slot: the CUDA mul_mat_id (MMQ)
leaves it out, op_params[2] = 1 on the down projection zeroes its rows of dst, and the mask
goes away. ids_src1 is filled with -1 for the quantize kernels, which now skip those rows
(through a signed cast: the old conditional promoted -1 to 4294967295), and the generic
mul_mat_id path reads a zero row for them.

Exact: KL against the build without it sits at the noise floor of the base file (max
0.000058, same top token 100%), MUL_MAT_ID 877/877. It does not speed prompts up on this
machine: the removed compute was hidden under the next wave's loads, and the disk is the
limit. At -ub 2048 the CUDA VMM pool then fails to grow on an 8.9K prompt
(cuMemSetAccess: not ready), hence off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
